    {
      "id": "s0020",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "DESCRIPTION",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0021",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Mutt is a small but very powerful text based program for reading and sending electronic mail under unix operating systems, including support for color terminals, MIME, OpenPGP, and a threaded sorting mode.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0022",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]]: This manual page gives a brief overview of the [[p1]] executable command line options. A copy of the full manual is located in [[p2]], in text, HTML, and/or PDF format. Please refer to the manual to learn how to use and configure Mutt.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "Note"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "mutt"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "@docdir@"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0023",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "OPTIONS",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0024",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]][[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-A"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "alias"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0025",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Print an expanded version of the given [[p0]] and exit.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "alias"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0026",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]][[p1]] file ... [[p2]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-a"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "<em>"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "</em>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0027",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Attach a [[p0]] using MIME. Separating [[p1]] and [[p2]] arguments with “[[p3]]” is mandatory. For example:",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "file"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "file"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "to-addr"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "text": "--"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0028",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The [[p0]] option must be placed at the end of command line options.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-a"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0029",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]][[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-b"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "bcc-addr"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0030",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Specify a blind carbon copy (BCC) address.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0031",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]][[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-c"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "cc-addr"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0032",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Specify a carbon copy (CC) address.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0033",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]][[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-d"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "level"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0034",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "If Mutt was compiled with [[p0]] log debugging output to [[p1]]. [[p2]] can range from -5 to 5 and affects verbosity. A value of zero disables debugging. A value less than zero disables automatic log file rotation; the log level is then its absolute value. A value of 2 (-2) is recommended for most diagnosis.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "+DEBUG"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "~/.muttdebug0"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "Level"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0035",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-D"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0036",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Print the value of all configuration options to stdout.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0037",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-E"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0038",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Edit the [[p0]] file specified by [[p1]] or [[p2]] file specified by [[p3]] during message composition.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "draft"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "-H"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "include"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "text": "-i"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0039",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]][[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-e"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "command"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0040",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Specify a configuration [[p0]] to be run after processing of initialization files.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "command"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0041",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]][[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-f"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "mailbox"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0042",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Specify a [[p0]] to load.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "mailbox"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0043",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]][[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-F"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "rcfile"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0044",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Use [[p0]] instead of the user configuration file.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "rcfile"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0045",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-h"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0046",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Display a short option summary and exit.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0047",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]][[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-H"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "draft"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0048",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Specify a [[p0]] file which contains header and body to use to send a message. If [[p1]] is “[[p2]]”, then data is read from stdin. The draft file is expected to contain just an RFC822 email — headers and a body. Although it is not an mbox file, if an mbox \"[[p3]]\" line is present, it will be silently discarded. Draft files are processed the same in interactive and batch mode; they are not passed through untouched. For example, encrypted draft files will be decrypted.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "draft"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "draft"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "-"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "text": "From"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0049",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]][[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-i"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "include"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0050",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Specify an [[p0]] file to be inserted into the body of a message. Ignored if [[p1]] is set. If [[p2]] is “[[p3]]”, then data is read from stdin.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "include"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "-H"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "include"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "text": "-"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0051",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]][[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-m"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "type"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0052",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Specify a default mailbox [[p0]] for newly created folders. Can be one of the following: mbox, MMDF, MH or Maildir. See also [[p1]] in the manual.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "type"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "$mbox_type"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0053",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0054",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Do not read the system-wide Muttrc configuration file.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0055",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-p"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0056",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Resume a postponed message. Exit immediately if there are no postponed messages.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0057",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]][[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-Q"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "variable"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0058",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Query a configuration [[p0]]. The query is performed after all configuration files have been parsed, and any [[p1]] given on the command line have been executed.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "variable"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "commands"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0059",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-R"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0060",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Open a mailbox in read-only mode.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0061",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]][[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-s"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "subject"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0062",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Specify the [[p0]] of the message. Must be enclosed in quotes if it contains spaces.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "subject"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0063",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-v"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0064",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Display the Mutt version number and compile-time definitions.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0065",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-vv"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0066",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Display license and copyright information.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0067",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-x"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0068",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Emulate the [[p0]](1) compose mode.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "mailx"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0069",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-y"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0070",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Start Mutt with a listing of all mailboxes specified by the [[p0]] configuration command.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "mailboxes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0071",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-z"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0072",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Exit immediately with code 1 if [[p0]] specified by [[p1]] does not contain any messages.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "mailbox"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "-f"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0073",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "-Z"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0074",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Open the first mailbox specified by the [[p0]] configuration command which contains new mail. Exit immediately with code 1 if there is no new mail in any of them.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "mailboxes"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0075",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "--"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0076",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Treat remaining arguments as [[p0]] even if they start with a dash. See also [[p1]] above. [[p2]] can be a local or network mail address as well as mailto: URL.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "to-addr"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "-a"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "To-addr"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0077",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "ENVIRONMENT",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0078",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "EDITOR, VISUAL",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0079",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Specifies the editor to use when composing messages. If both EDITOR and VISUAL are set, VISUAL takes precedence. If neither EDITOR nor VISUAL are set, the default is [[p0]](1).",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "vi"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0080",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "EGDSOCKET, RANDFILE",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0081",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Paths used to initialize the random engine for SSL library.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0082",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "EMAIL",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0083",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The user's e-mail address.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0084",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "HOME",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0085",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Full path of the user's home directory.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0086",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "MAIL",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0087",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Full path of the user's spool mailbox.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0088",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "MAILDIR",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0089",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Full path of the user's spool mailbox if MAIL is unset. Commonly used when the spool mailbox is a [[p0]](5) folder.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "maildir"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0090",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "MAILCAPS",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0091",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Path to search for mailcap files.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0092",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "MM_NOASK",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0093",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "If this variable is set, mailcap are always used without prompting first.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0094",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "PGPPATH",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0095",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Directory in which the user's PGP public keyring can be found. When used with the original PGP program, mutt and [[p0]](1) rely on this being set.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "mutt_pgpring"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0096",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "REPLYTO",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0097",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Default Reply-To address.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0098",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "TMPDIR",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0099",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Directory in which temporary files are created. If unset, [[p0]] is used for $tmpdir, and [[p1]] is used for $tmpdraftdir. See also the $tmpdir and $tmpdraftdir configuration variables.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "/tmp"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "/var/tmp"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0100",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "LC_ALL, LC_CTYPE, LANG",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0101",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Used to determine charset and locale to use.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0102",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "TEXTDOMAINDIR",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0103",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Directory containing translation files. If set, this path overwrite the Mutt installation directory. Used for testing translation changes.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0104",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "FILES",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0105",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "~/.muttrc"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0106",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "~/.mutt/muttrc"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0107",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mutt/muttrc"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0108",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "User configuration files.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0109",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]@sysconfdir@/Muttrc or @pkgdatadir@/Muttrc[[p1]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "<em>"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "</em>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0110",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "System-wide configuration file.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0111",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "/tmp/muttXXXXXX"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0112",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Temporary files created by Mutt.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0113",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "~/.muttdebug0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0114",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "File containing debugging output. Log files are automatically rotated by [[p0]] changing the number at the end. See [[p1]] option above.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "mutt"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "-d"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0115",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "~/.mailcap"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0116",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "User definition for handling non-text MIME types.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0117",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "@sysconfdir@/mailcap"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0118",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "System definition for handling non-text MIME types.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0119",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "~/.mime.types"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0120",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "User's personal mapping between MIME types and file extensions.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0121",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "@sysconfdir@/mime.types"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0122",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "System mapping between MIME types and file extensions.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0123",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "@bindir@/mutt_dotlock"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0124",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The privileged dotlocking program.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0125",
      "kind": "term",
      "text": "[[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "@docdir@/manual.txt"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0126",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Mutt manual.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0127",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "BUGS",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0128",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "None. Mutts have fleas, not bugs.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0129",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "FLEAS",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0130",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Suspend/resume while editing a file with an external editor does not work under SunOS 4.x if you use the curses lib in /usr/5lib. It [[p0]] work with the S-Lang library, however.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "does"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0131",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Resizing the screen while using an external pager causes Mutt to go haywire on some systems.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0132",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Suspend/resume does not work under Ultrix.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0133",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The help line for the index menu is not updated if you change the bindings for one of the functions listed while Mutt is running.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0134",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "For a more up-to-date list of bugs, errm, fleas, please visit the mutt project's bug tracking system under https://gitlab.com/muttmua/mutt/issues. NOTE: The bug tracking system is not meant for feature requests. These should go to the mutt-dev mailing list, see section 1.2 Mailing Lists of the manual for details.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0135",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "NO WARRANTIES",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0136",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the GNU General Public License for more details.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0137",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "SEE ALSO",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0138",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "[[p0]](1), [[p1]](1), [[p2]](1), [[p3]](1), [[p4]](1), [[p5]](1), [[p6]](3), [[p7]](3), [[p8]](5), [[p9]](5), [[p10]](5), [[p11]](5), [[p12]](5)",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "text": "mutt_dotlock"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "text": "mutt_pgpring"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p2]]",
          "text": "pgpewrap"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p3]]",
          "text": "sendmail"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p4]]",
          "text": "smail"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p5]]",
          "text": "smime_keys"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p6]]",
          "text": "curses"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p7]]",
          "text": "ncurses"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p8]]",
          "text": "mailcap"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p9]]",
          "text": "maildir"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p10]]",
          "text": "mbox"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p11]]",
          "text": "mmdf"
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p12]]",
          "text": "muttrc"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0139",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Mutt Home Page: http://www.mutt.org/",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0140",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Mutt manual",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0141",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "RFC5322 — Internet Message Format: https://tools.ietf.org/rfcmarkup/5322 (obsoletes RFC2822 and RFC822)",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0142",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "AUTHOR",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0143",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Michael Elkins, and others. Use <mutt-dev@mutt.org> to contact the developers.",
      "protected": []
    }
  ]
}
